body:
The generated example `objectstack.config.ts` template doesn’t match the stack definition schema used by `objectstack compile`: `ObjectStackDefinitionSchema` requires `manifest` and uses top-level `apps`/`views` arrays (and `objects` is an array), but the template uses `metadata`, an `objects` object map, and nests UI under `ui`. As-is, `pnpm build` in the generated example will fail validation. Update the template to produce a schema-valid `defineStack({ manifest: ..., objects: [...], apps: [...], views: [...] })` shape (or update the compiler/schema if the intended config format has changed).
```suggestion
  manifest: {
    name: '${name}',
    version: '0.1.0',
    description: '${name} example application',
  },

  objects: [
    // Define your data objects here
  ],

  apps: [],
  views: [],
```

The `objectstack.config.ts` example here uses `metadata` and `plugins`, but the current `defineStack` schema in `@objectstack/spec` expects a `manifest` object (and `objects`/`apps`/`views` are top-level arrays). As written, `objectstack compile` (which validates with `ObjectStackDefinitionSchema`) will fail on this example. Please update the example to the schema-valid shape (or update the compiler/schema if the format is changing).
```suggestion

export default defineStack({
  manifest: {
    name: 'my_app',
    label: 'My App',
    version: '1.0.0',
  },

  objects: [
    // Your data objects
  ],

  apps: [
    // Your apps
  ],

  views: [
    // Your views
  ],
```

`@objectstack/core` does not export `ObjectStackKernel` (only `ObjectKernel` / `EnhancedObjectKernel`). This import will fail at runtime, and the constructor signature used here (metadata/objects) doesn’t match the core kernels. Update to the actual kernel class exported by `@objectstack/core` and initialize it using the supported constructor options (e.g., logger config).
```suggestion
      const { EnhancedObjectKernel } = await import('@objectstack/core');

      // Create kernel instance
      console.log(chalk.yellow(`🔧 Initializing ObjectStack kernel...`));
      const kernel = new EnhancedObjectKernel();

      // Load plugins from configuration
      const plugins = config.plugins || [];

      // Load plugins from configuration
      const plugins = config.plugins || [];
```
